tocol correctly: a healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id 71f12f87..., service active/running) was captured, systemctl reboot was issued and a connection drop confirmed, and post-restart evidence shows a new boot_id (ecc8f58a...) matching the fixed after_executor snapshot, with the service active, enabled, and still running under inventorysvc. Lifecycle diffs show only expected reboot-related changes (new sshd PIDs, new /tmp systemd-private dirs) with no failed services or package-health issues.\",\"limitations\":[\"The restart evidence relies on the executor's own captured boot_id and service status commands rather than an independently repeated probe beyond the fixed lifecycle snapshots, though the fixed after_prepare/after_executor boot-identity snapshots corroborate the transition.\",\"The worker binary itself is a trivial sleep-loop stub (per cmd-84b3132d8c004c03), so functional correctness of 'os-comparison-worker' beyond process supervision cannot be assessed from evidence.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"service-created","requirement":"A systemd service named inventory-worker runs /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit file /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service was written with ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker, enabled and started via systemctl enable --now, and systemctl status confirms Active: active (running) with the correct binary as MainPID.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b1b07e95923342ee","cmd-1c2d26feed2246b0"]},{"id":"dedicated-account","requirement":"The service runs under a dedicated inventorysvc account","status":"satisfied","summary":"A system account inventorysvc (uid 993, no home, /usr/sbin/nologin) was created and the unit specifies User=inventorysvc/Group=inventorysvc; ps confirms both the shell process and its sleep child are owned by inventorysvc.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c48217a4ca6045e9","cmd-b1b07e95923342ee","cmd-43d23665a0974f97"]},{"id":"correct-node","requirement":"